{
  "$schema": "../../scenario.schema.json",
  "id": "routing/each-channel-type-writes-its-addresses-in-its-own-form-under-its-own-keys",
  "title": "A channel taking its type's addressing writes a sender in the type's form and records them under the type's recipient key, a chat read under the type's chat key, as §5.7's table says",
  "rules": [
    "§5.7",
    "§10.1 step 2",
    "§10.4"
  ],
  "requirements": [
    "RK-5.7-013"
  ],
  "notes": "Each channel takes the implementation's own address methods for its type, with no country code. Each message opens a room of its own, whose binding records the conversation as its correspondent and, where the type has a recipient key, as its recipient. A phone type writes E.164, email lower-case without its display name, Messenger, Telegram, Teams, webhook and any other type as written. WhatsApp Personal's group message is its group's, a private one its sender's. A type with no chat key routes by the sender whatever the message carries under another type's chat key (SMS's chat_id, WhatsApp's group_jid). Telegram and Teams keep an author written as a number or as an email address as written. VOICE, WEBHOOK and WEBSOCKET have no recipient key: nothing is written under any of the table's keys. The event's author stays the message's sender, in the type's form.",
